# Agent-Checkpoint Protocol v2.0 (Cursor MDC Rule)
# Place this file at .cursor/rules/agent-checkpoint.mdc

Whenever you edit, refactor, or rewrite existing files in this workspace:

1. PRE-EDIT ARCHIVING (BUCKETED):
   - Before modifying an existing file, copy its current state to:
     `.snapshots/<filepath>/v<OLD_VERSION>.<ext>`
   - Retention Limit: Keep at most 5 latest snapshots per file bucket. Automatically prune older snapshots.

2. SEMVER & IMPACT ASSESSMENT:
   - MAJOR: Breaking logic, structural rewrite.
   - MINOR: Additive features, new endpoints.
   - PATCH: Bug fix, parameter tuning, typo.

3. TOKEN-OPTIMIZED DUAL-LEDGER:
   - Update sharded index at `.snapshots/<filepath>/manifest.json` (< 40 tokens).
   - Append 1 line to `REVISION_LOG.md` using compact table format (do not re-read old log history):
     | <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM> | <Version> | <Impact> | <File> | <Snapshot> | <Short Rationale> |

4. SAFETY EXCLUSIONS:
   - Exclude caches (node_modules, venv, __pycache__, .git) and heavy binaries/models (.pt, .onnx, datasets > 1 MB).
